+# Design follow-up after PRs 944–948
+
+The 2026-10-16 audit inspected main
+`ddb8ed9504beb04c06bfe11821ebcafffa332714` after the previous five findings were
+implemented. It identified three remaining representation issues: duplicate
+project roots in normalized configuration, early conversion of analyzer
+operators to strings, and independently specified process-dispatch identity.
+Issues [949](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/949),
+[950](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/950), and
+[951](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/951) contain the evidence and
+acceptance conditions. These are proposed improvements, not implemented
+contracts or reproduced runtime failures. Compatibility preservation is not a
+requirement for the root consolidation.[^post948-design-audit]
+
+The audit distinguishes necessary lifecycle observations and derived indexes
+from duplicated authority. Its 7.5/10 score supports six diagnostic rows; local
+synchronization obligations remain and design-time allocation was not measured.
+No new runtime suite, mutation campaign or Lean proof was run. The record
+includes rejected candidates, review passes and verification limits.
+[^post948-design-audit]
+
+[^post948-design-audit]: [Post-948 design audit](../../maintenance/2026-10-16-post948-design-audit.md).
